{
  "feature_name": "Convert File To / From Base64",
  "value_prop": "Two new StudioWeb API Workflow activities that round-trip files and Base64 strings, with a typed, reusable output — no more hand-written conversion glue.",
  "persona": "Developers and makers building API workflows in StudioWeb",
  "when_to_use": "When a customer's API sends or receives file data encoded as Base64 — document services, e-signature, image upload/download, or email attachments.",
  "talking_points": [
    "Two drag-in activities: Convert File To Base64 and Convert File From Base64.",
    "Convert File From Base64 takes a required Base64 string plus optional File name and MIME type.",
    "Both surface a typed output (a Job Attachment) that downstream activities can consume.",
    "The output pill stays visible while you edit inputs; every property round-trips on save and reload.",
    "Ships behind a preview feature flag, with the full activity suite green (16/16)."
  ],
  "objections": [
    {
      "q": "Couldn't you already do this with an expression?",
      "a": "You could hand-write conversion glue, but it wasn't typed and the result wasn't reusable. These are first-class activities whose output is a typed Job Attachment downstream activities can consume."
    },
    {
      "q": "Is it production-ready?",
      "a": "It ships behind a preview feature flag with the full activity suite green (16/16) and properties that round-trip on save and reload. Executor changes are tracked separately in API-Workflow #679."
    },
    {
      "q": "What exactly can it convert?",
      "a": "It round-trips any file to a Base64 string and back — Convert File From Base64 also lets you set the decoded file's name and MIME type."
    }
  ],
  "music_mood": "uplifting",
  "scenes": [
